# Line endings are part of this repository's contract, not a local preference.
#
# Everything is stored with LF, and this file makes git check it out with LF on
# Windows too. Without it, a Windows clone with the default `core.autocrlf=true`
# rewrites every text file to CRLF on checkout, and three things break — all of
# them confusingly, and none of them at the point of the change:
#
#   1. **Migration checksums.** scripts/migrate.ts hashes each migration's raw
#      *bytes* (`createHash("sha256").update(contents)`), and forward-only
#      migrations are immutable once applied. A CRLF checkout changes every
#      byte count, so an already-migrated database fails the next boot with
#      `migration_checksum_mismatch` on a file nobody edited.
#   2. **`.mjs`/`.ts` files whose first line is a shebang.** A trailing CR on
#      `#!/usr/bin/env node` makes vite's transform fail with
#      "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" — which is reported against
#      the *importing test file*, not the script that actually has the CR.
#      (scripts/verify-production-deploy.mjs, imported by
#      src/lib/production-deploy-verification.test.ts.)
#   3. **Shell scripts.** docker-entrypoint.sh runs in a Linux container; with
#      CRLF the kernel looks for an interpreter named "/bin/sh\r".
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` normalises on commit and checks out LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only files that a person edits in a Windows editor, and that Windows
# tooling is happiest reading as CRLF. None of them are hashed or executed by
# the Linux image.
*.bat     text eol=crlf
*.cmd     text eol=crlf
*.ps1     text eol=crlf
*.vbs     text eol=crlf

# Always binary — never touch the bytes.
*.png     binary
*.ico     binary
*.woff2   binary
*.7z      binary
*.zip     binary
*.exe     binary

# Stored with CRLF and marked binary before this file existed (git reports it
# as `-text`). It asserts on an embedded PEM-ish fixture, so leave its bytes
# exactly as they are rather than renormalising them.
src/lib/github-app-token.test.ts -text
